\f0\fs24 \cf0 Installing LittleFS uploader on Arduino IDE\
\
1. Download the plugin                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                        \
  Go to the https://github.com/earlephilhower/arduino-littlefs-upload/releases and download the .vsix file (latest is   \
  v1.6.3).                                                                                                              \
\
  2. Copy to plugins folder                                                                                             \
                                                                                                                        \
  mkdir -p ~/.arduinoIDE/plugins                                                                                        \
  cp ~/Downloads/arduino-littlefs-upload-*.vsix ~/.arduinoIDE/plugins/\
\
  3. Restart Arduino IDE\
\
  Fully quit and reopen it.\
\
  4. Upload your data/ folder\
\
  - Make sure your .pd files are in the sketch's data/ folder (you already have this)\
  - Close the Serial Monitor (important \'97 upload fails if it's open)\
  - Press Cmd + Shift + P to open the Command Palette\
  - Type and select "Upload LittleFS to Pico/ESP8266/ESP32"\
\
  That flashes the contents of data/ directly to the LittleFS partition. Your sketch then just calls\
  Pd.openPatch("simple-phasor.pd") and the file is already there \'97 no embedding, no python script, no serial upload.\
\
  If you go this route, you can simplify the sketch by removing all the embedded_patches.h and writeEmbeddedPatches()\
  code \'97 the patches are already on flash before the sketch even boots.\
\
  One caveat: you need a partition scheme with a LittleFS partition. In Arduino IDE under Tools > Partition Scheme, pick\
   something like "Default 4MB with spiffs (1.2MB APP/1.5MB SPIFFS)" \'97 despite the name, LittleFS uses the same\
  partition.\
\
  Sources:\
  - https://github.com/earlephilhower/arduino-littlefs-upload\
  - https://randomnerdtutorials.com/arduino-ide-2-install-esp32-littlefs/\
\
